{"source":"github","project_id":"model-implementation-principles","target":"tidymodels/model-implementation-principles","id":"pr/12","ref":12,"title":"Add note about subclassing","description":"An attempt to avoid the special hells accompanying subclassing `lm`, `anova`, or similar. Unfortunately, many of the canonical \"copy this structure\" functions in `MASS` do this and then break down the line.\r\n\r\nActually, I think is a really good rule of thumb that we should make sure to implement in `parsnip`: only create model objects from constructors/validators. We should probably also provide constructors and validators for `parsnip` objects in if we want them to be extensible. cc @DavisVaughan ","published_at":"2018-11-22T04:56:57Z","updated_at":"2020-08-07T14:01:12Z","url":"https://github.com/tidymodels/model-implementation-principles/pull/12","type":"pr","extra":{"author":"alexpghayes","merged_at":"2020-08-07T14:01:12Z","state":"MERGED"}}
